    "uri": "http://100.70.188.20:56741/files/90d2fbaf34e6/ai-reflection-v1.pdf",
    "text": "This is wrong. The point is that the actively pursued criterion is overlapping with what I actually want enough to deliver a useful end-result. It is not necessary, nor is it likely, that the agent actually pursues the same goal as I described. It is also demonstratedly true that agents can describe what goal I described, and yet still pursue something else. So wrong inference of a goal is not the issue, it is \"wrong picking of a goal\". This is standard alignment theory, and apparently now manifests for ambitious goals in an observable manner in publicly released models. ",
